config VIDEO_MTK_SCAM
	tristate "MediaTek MT6589 sensor-CAM adaptor"
	depends on HAS_IOMEM && OF
	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK || COMPILE_TEST
	select VIDEO_V4L2_SUBDEV_API
	select V4L2_ASYNC
	select VIDEO_MTK_CAM_GRAPH
	help
	  Say Y here if you want to use the MediaTek MT6589 sensor-CAM
	  (SCAM) adaptor.

	  The SCAM blocks sit between each CSI-2 receiver and the CAM/ISP.
	  They carry the unpacked byte stream and the frame/line
	  synchronisation across to the ISP and raise the frame and line
	  interrupts the ISP uses.

	  WARNING: this driver is partial.  The reset/enable/size path is
	  implemented and it will probe, but the pixel-format handling and
	  the media-controller glue towards the ISP are not written, and
	  there is no vendor reference driver for this block in the
	  available tree.  It will not yet produce frames.  See the file
	  header and README.md.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
	  will be called mtk-scam.
